<title>GERMANY: East German Feb industry orders rise 4.9 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>East German Feb industry orders rise 4.9 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +4.9	 -0.8	 +7.8</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+8.6	+11.5	 -2.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		138.0	131.5	127.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Feb 97    Jan 97    Feb 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +8.1	 -5.7     155.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Jan/Feb 97 with Nov/Dec 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +2.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Jan/Feb 97 with Jan/Feb 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +7.9</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +1.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +37.7</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +11.3</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +5.2</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +1.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
